WEBVTT

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.450
- Input failure.
- Input failure.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.428
Input failure.

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:41.163
Our link to the collective
has been severed.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.004
Initiate secondary protocols.

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.246
The vessel's transwarp chamber

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.940
is approaching
critical pressure.

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:50.607
We must evacuate this area.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:51.980
Agreed.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:52.984
No directional...

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.247
coordinates are available.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.287
...coordinates
are available.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:57.953
That way.

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:58.956
Bearing 301.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:00:59.992
Agreed.

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.528
Bring that drone.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.041
Captain's Log, Stardate 53049.2.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.051
We've docked
at the Markonian Outpost

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:07.677
and agreed to mutual visits,

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:10.450
so I'm allowing shore leave
to anyone who wants it.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:14.050
Commander Tuvok has objected
to taking on too many visitors.

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:15.389
But, security issues aside,

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.588
I'm looking forward
to a cultural exchange

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.222
and making some new friends.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.095
Pardon me.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.263
Excuse me.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.636
Careful, careful.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:28.969
Excuse me.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:32.643
Watch it!

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.145
Excuse me.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.306
Captain?

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.078
I'll be right with you.

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:45.322
The station manager didn't tell
me the vines were prehensile.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:48.189
I went to put some water
in the pot and it grabbed me.

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:50.456
This is a gift
from the Kinbori Delegation.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.588
I don't know its name,

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:54.155
only that it's used
in one of their sacred games

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.258
and it's very heavy.

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:57.098
Well, put it down anywhere.

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.134
Thank the Kinbori for me,

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:07.304
and give them
a token of our esteem.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.042
I already gave them
a Voyager medallion.

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:11.811
They seemed appreciative.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.317
Come in.

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:17.818
Doesn't it look like

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.154
Christmas morning
in here, Commander?

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:21.784
You have to admit the generosity

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.453
of our guests is
very impressive.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.793
As is their proclivity
for criminal behavior.

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.389
This morning's security report.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.059
Broken ODN line...

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:31.035
some missing personal items...

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.731
a damaged scanner relay.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.397
All in all, not that bad.

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:36.567
There is a second page
to the report.

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:39.578
Well, some
of these incidents

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:41.477
are a little more serious.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:44.744
But on balance, I still think
we did the right thing.

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.648
There is a third page.

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:51.247
Come on, Tuvok, after all the
xenophobic races we've run into

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:53.155
don't you find it
just a little refreshing

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:55.956
to meet some people
who value openness and freedom?

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.290
Well, as far as I'm concerned,

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.558
opening the ship has been
a fascinating experience

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:00.963
and an unqualified success.

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:02.001
I'm very pleased.

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:03.126
Me, too.

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:05.762
I am pleased
that you are pleased.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:07.066
If you'll excuse me.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.072
Tuvok...

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:10.109
please accept this
token of our esteem.

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:14.570
Oh, no.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.547
It's got me by the hair.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.912
Now it's 12:45.

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:25.115
If you're hungry,
you may eat without me.

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:27.421
You said we'd have
lunch together.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:28.858
I haven't completed
my analysis

00:05:28.928 --> 00:05:30.828
of the station's power
conversion matrix.

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:32.762
How long is it gonna take?

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:33.924
Several hours.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.059
Seven, you promised.

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:40.198
Very well.

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.650
I think it's even more crowded
than this morning.

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:53.947
Yes.

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.180
Excuse us. Excuse us.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:58.883
Please, we're trying to get
through to the turbolift.

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:00.755
Excuse us.

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:02.556
Stand aside!

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:06.994
Thank you.

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:15.299
I'm sorry, but there's
no more Marsupial Surprise.

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:18.606
We only had two kilos
of pouches to begin with

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:19.906
and it's all gone!

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:21.877
Now, how about some pizza, huh?

00:06:21.948 --> 00:06:25.850
She's... a Shivolian, right?

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:26.907
Correct.

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:29.112
Species 521?

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:31.019
Your mother
would not approve of you

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.614
memorizing Borg designations.

00:06:32.692 --> 00:06:33.624
I don't approve either.

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:34.921
We've discussed
the impropriety

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:37.427
of you emulating the Borg.

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:38.794
Sorry.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.428
I'm finished.

00:06:42.502 --> 00:06:43.867
We just sat down.

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:47.201
I do not enjoy crowds.

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:48.501
But you were in the collective.

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:49.768
Wasn't that like a big crowd?

00:06:49.842 --> 00:06:53.334
Which is why
I do not enjoy them now.

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:55.381
Oh. I'm sorry.
I didn't realize that.

00:06:55.448 --> 00:06:56.380
Let's go.

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:57.416
Excuse me.

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:00.879
Are you Seven of Nine?

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:02.477
Yes.

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:25.372
You okay?

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:27.845
These are Borg synaptic relays

00:07:27.914 --> 00:07:30.075
from my original unimatrix.

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:32.014
These are yours?

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.517
Where did you acquire them?

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:37.386
A trader from Orendal V.

00:07:37.457 --> 00:07:39.891
I was told
you are a former Borg drone

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:42.393
and might be interested
in acquiring these pieces.

00:07:42.462 --> 00:07:44.930
I'll take them.

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:46.430
Captain Janeway will provide you

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:48.660
with whatever monetary
reimbursement you require.

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:50.668
Agreed.

00:07:51.838 --> 00:07:55.103
I must examine these items
more closely.

00:07:55.174 --> 00:07:56.141
Okay.

00:07:57.677 --> 00:07:58.905
What's your name?

00:08:02.148 --> 00:08:04.013
That was rude.

00:08:08.588 --> 00:08:10.852
Stage two is complete.

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:12.254
She has the relays.

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:13.485
She's going to study them.

00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:16.687
Her regeneration alcove
is in Cargo Bay 2.

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:18.127
That's where she'll go.

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:20.290
We should prepare
for stage three.

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:21.731
Agreed.

00:08:21.801 --> 00:08:23.894
There's consensus.

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:25.994
Rendezvous at my coordinates

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:28.700
and stand by
to penetrate their security.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:45.919
Error.

00:08:46.025 --> 00:08:47.458
Explain.

00:08:48.561 --> 00:08:52.224
We shouldn't be desecrating
the body of this drone.

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:54.823
It is against the will
of Brothara.

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:56.493
Who is Brothara?

00:08:56.569 --> 00:09:00.630
Brothara: A supernatural
deity worshipped

00:09:00.706 --> 00:09:02.264
by Species 571.

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:06.667
I am a member of Species 571.

00:09:06.746 --> 00:09:08.873
You're being confused
by irrelevant data.

00:09:08.948 --> 00:09:10.108
Ignore it.

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:13.174
You said, "I am
a member of Species 571."

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:15.345
Do you consider yourself
an individual?

00:09:17.523 --> 00:09:18.990
There are no individuals here.

00:09:19.058 --> 00:09:19.990
We are Borg.

00:09:20.059 --> 00:09:22.391
- Agreed.
- Agreed.

00:09:22.461 --> 00:09:23.723
Agreed.

00:09:23.796 --> 00:09:26.356
Resume constructing
the communications beacon.

00:09:43.749 --> 00:09:46.843
It looks like
a standard Borg synaptic relay.

00:09:46.919 --> 00:09:49.820
There must be something more.

00:09:49.889 --> 00:09:52.119
When I first came
into contact with it,

00:09:52.191 --> 00:09:55.058
I was overwhelmed
with images, memories, sounds.

00:09:55.127 --> 00:09:58.528
Sounds like a perfectly natural
reaction to me.

00:09:58.598 --> 00:10:01.499
That was part
your old unimatrix, right?

00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:03.535
Well, isn't it
at least possible

00:10:03.603 --> 00:10:06.595
that what you experienced
was simply nostalgia?

00:10:06.672 --> 00:10:08.640
You know, sentimental
feelings about the past.

00:10:08.708 --> 00:10:10.733
I know what nostalgia is,

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:13.210
but I have no feelings
about the past.

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:14.211
Okay.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:18.273
I think I've done
all I can here.

00:10:19.452 --> 00:10:20.476
Lieutenant...

00:10:22.588 --> 00:10:26.354
you were trying to help.

00:10:26.425 --> 00:10:27.949
I appreciate that.

00:10:28.094 --> 00:10:30.426
Anytime.

00:10:30.496 --> 00:10:35.195
Oh, and, um, you may not
be nostalgic about the past,

00:10:35.267 --> 00:10:38.964
but I'd say you definitely
have feelings about it.

00:10:39.105 --> 00:10:40.367
Strong ones.

00:10:50.449 --> 00:10:52.576
Their security protocols
are formidable.

00:10:52.652 --> 00:10:54.085
We may not have enough time.

00:10:54.153 --> 00:10:56.553
I'm worried
about Seven of Nine.

00:10:56.622 --> 00:10:57.987
We should reexamine

00:10:58.057 --> 00:10:59.524
the question
of simply asking...

00:10:59.592 --> 00:11:00.991
You know what her
reactions will be.

00:11:01.127 --> 00:11:02.219
She won't help us
because she...

00:11:02.294 --> 00:11:03.761
We've been through all that.

00:11:03.829 --> 00:11:06.821
She could be
permanently injured.

00:11:06.899 --> 00:11:08.696
I don't want to harm...

00:11:08.768 --> 00:11:09.735
Enough!

00:11:12.471 --> 00:11:15.304
We need consensus.

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:20.244
We can't act without it.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.774
I know.

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:27.944
So, then it's up to you.

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:30.580
Do we proceed or not?

00:11:32.291 --> 00:11:33.622
Yes.

00:11:36.295 --> 00:11:40.095
We... I apologize
for my indecision.

00:11:41.667 --> 00:11:43.157
Apologies are irrelevant!

00:11:47.006 --> 00:11:49.497
Computer, begin
multipolar analysis.

00:11:49.575 --> 00:11:51.202
Analysis underway.

00:11:51.277 --> 00:11:52.801
Time to completion?

00:11:52.878 --> 00:11:54.846
Five hours, 17 minutes.

00:12:08.761 --> 00:12:11.195
She's regenerating.

00:12:11.263 --> 00:12:14.232
Begin rerouting
their internal sensors.

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:18.168
Rerouting sensor input
to secondary processors.

00:12:45.631 --> 00:12:46.620
Hold.

00:12:49.435 --> 00:12:51.164
What have you got?

00:12:51.237 --> 00:12:54.206
There's a power fluctuation
in the security grid.

00:13:12.291 --> 00:13:14.191
All we know is that we've
got a security breach.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:15.284
We don't know where.

00:13:22.735 --> 00:13:24.225
Ready.

00:13:24.303 --> 00:13:26.271
Insert the interlink module.

00:13:31.443 --> 00:13:32.603
Ready.

00:13:37.716 --> 00:13:40.014
He's still worried
about injuring her.

00:13:45.925 --> 00:13:49.053
If we fail, we'll never
become individuals.

00:13:49.128 --> 00:13:50.959
We have to remember that.

00:13:55.768 --> 00:13:57.360
There is consensus.

00:14:07.813 --> 00:14:10.077
I've found her memory files.

00:14:10.149 --> 00:14:11.776
She's aware of our presence.

00:14:11.851 --> 00:14:14.911
She's trying
to regain consciousness.

00:14:14.987 --> 00:14:15.919
We must abort.

00:14:16.055 --> 00:14:17.989
No! We're too close.

00:14:20.659 --> 00:14:23.127
I will not comply.

00:14:58.197 --> 00:15:02.634
I have performed
this action before.

00:15:02.701 --> 00:15:05.295
I was with my father.

00:15:05.371 --> 00:15:07.532
He was a tall man.

00:15:07.606 --> 00:15:10.769
I have a... similar memory.

00:15:10.843 --> 00:15:13.004
But I was in a house

00:15:13.078 --> 00:15:15.569
and the fire was in a hearth.

00:15:15.648 --> 00:15:17.946
The biomatter is ready.

00:15:28.193 --> 00:15:33.028
It tastes similar
to a bird I once ate.

00:15:33.098 --> 00:15:34.929
I used to prepare food...

00:15:35.067 --> 00:15:36.932
for...

00:15:37.069 --> 00:15:38.502
my parents.

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:41.801
They lived...
in a small building

00:15:41.874 --> 00:15:43.705
by...

00:15:43.776 --> 00:15:46.210
a river.

00:15:46.278 --> 00:15:47.836
I used to be...

00:15:47.913 --> 00:15:50.279
afraid of the dark.

00:15:50.349 --> 00:15:52.544
Just before I was assimilated,
I was...

00:15:52.618 --> 00:15:56.952
eating with a group of men.

00:15:57.089 --> 00:16:01.526
We... worked in numbers.

00:16:01.593 --> 00:16:02.685
Mathematics.

00:16:02.761 --> 00:16:06.322
I... calculated equations
for another man.

00:16:06.398 --> 00:16:08.298
I have a name.

00:16:09.468 --> 00:16:11.060
It's...

00:16:11.136 --> 00:16:12.603
Marika.

00:16:16.342 --> 00:16:21.541
Marika Willkarah.

00:16:21.613 --> 00:16:23.808
Willkarah.

00:16:23.882 --> 00:16:26.578
Hello, Marika Willkarah.

00:16:27.987 --> 00:16:29.921
Her designation
is Three of Nine.

00:16:30.055 --> 00:16:31.920
I have a name.

00:16:32.057 --> 00:16:35.026
P'Chan.

00:16:35.094 --> 00:16:38.222
Son of Dornar and Ansha.

00:16:38.297 --> 00:16:41.460
My primary function
was to care for them.

00:16:41.533 --> 00:16:42.591
I was married.

00:16:42.668 --> 00:16:45.660
We were on a starship...

00:16:45.738 --> 00:16:47.262
the Excalibur.

00:16:47.339 --> 00:16:51.036
I worked in Engineering.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:53.738
This is not my hand.

00:16:53.812 --> 00:16:56.406
My parents... they're dead.

00:16:56.482 --> 00:16:58.609
The Borg killed them.

00:17:02.688 --> 00:17:04.713
I hate the Borg.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:07.315
This is counterproductive.

00:17:07.393 --> 00:17:09.884
We must delete
all irrelevant data.

00:17:10.029 --> 00:17:11.758
I want my hand back.

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:13.092
I was on duty...

00:17:13.165 --> 00:17:14.598
the night watch...

00:17:14.666 --> 00:17:17.567
when the Borg came...

00:17:17.636 --> 00:17:19.695
Oh, my God!

00:17:19.772 --> 00:17:23.469
Look at what they've...
done to me!

00:17:23.542 --> 00:17:26.033
These-these things
they put in my body!

00:17:26.111 --> 00:17:27.078
What have they done?

00:17:27.146 --> 00:17:29.011
Command override.

00:17:29.081 --> 00:17:30.275
Cease this interaction!

00:17:32.618 --> 00:17:34.085
Comply.

00:17:34.153 --> 00:17:37.919
We will not access
these memory files again.

00:17:38.023 --> 00:17:39.320
Initiate the prescribed

00:17:39.391 --> 00:17:42.224
maintenance and survival
protocols only.

00:17:42.294 --> 00:17:44.524
No further communication
is required,

00:17:44.596 --> 00:17:47.565
until we are reassimilated
into the collective.

00:17:47.633 --> 00:17:52.935
- Agreed.
- Agreed.

00:17:53.072 --> 00:17:54.903
Agreed.

00:18:01.647 --> 00:18:04.775
...but whoever removed their
implants was a poor surgeon.

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:07.284
Their internal organs were
damaged during the procedure

00:18:07.352 --> 00:18:09.547
and their bodies are
covered with scars.

00:18:09.621 --> 00:18:11.452
You said you recognized them.

00:18:11.523 --> 00:18:12.820
Not at first.

00:18:12.891 --> 00:18:15.382
But when they attempted
to access my memory files,

00:18:15.461 --> 00:18:17.258
I was momentarily linked
with them.

00:18:17.329 --> 00:18:18.421
Two of Nine.

00:18:18.497 --> 00:18:20.522
Three of Nine.

00:18:20.599 --> 00:18:21.827
Four of Nine.

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:24.494
We were all members
of the same unimatrix.

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:27.130
Do you know why they were trying
to access your memories?

00:18:27.206 --> 00:18:28.468
No.

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:30.440
How long have they
been disconnected

00:18:30.509 --> 00:18:31.601
from the collective?

00:18:31.677 --> 00:18:32.735
Three or four months.

00:18:32.811 --> 00:18:35.405
However, they are still
connected to each other.

00:18:35.481 --> 00:18:38.109
Somehow, the left parietal
lobes of their brains

00:18:38.183 --> 00:18:41.175
have been transformed
into organic interlink nodes.

00:18:41.253 --> 00:18:43.312
They've become
linked together

00:18:43.388 --> 00:18:45.822
into a sort of collective triad.

00:18:45.891 --> 00:18:47.290
Revive them.

00:18:54.933 --> 00:18:56.730
I'm Captain Janeway.

00:18:56.802 --> 00:18:58.633
We know who you are,

00:18:58.704 --> 00:19:00.934
and we know
what you were trying to do.

00:19:01.073 --> 00:19:02.631
What we don't know is why.

00:19:02.708 --> 00:19:04.198
She has information
we need.

00:19:04.276 --> 00:19:05.641
What kind of information?

00:19:05.711 --> 00:19:07.042
We want to become...

00:19:07.112 --> 00:19:08.602
Individuals.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:10.875
You want to break
the neural link

00:19:10.949 --> 00:19:12.678
between the three of you?

00:19:12.751 --> 00:19:13.843
Wouldn't you?

00:19:13.919 --> 00:19:15.011
None of us is alone

00:19:15.087 --> 00:19:17.112
with our own thoughts,
our own feelings.

00:19:17.189 --> 00:19:18.554
Every day of my life is spent

00:19:18.624 --> 00:19:20.592
hearing their two voices
in my head.

00:19:20.659 --> 00:19:21.751
When we're asleep,

00:19:21.827 --> 00:19:23.419
we experience
each other's dreams.

00:19:23.495 --> 00:19:25.861
How's that different
from life in the collective?

00:19:25.931 --> 00:19:28.195
In the collective, there
are billions of voices.

00:19:28.267 --> 00:19:30.701
They become... white noise.

00:19:30.769 --> 00:19:32.532
But with only three...

00:19:32.604 --> 00:19:34.799
Each voice comes through
clearly.

00:19:34.873 --> 00:19:36.431
It has to stop.

00:19:36.508 --> 00:19:39.272
We must break the neural link.

00:19:39.344 --> 00:19:41.608
Doctor, is there anything
you can do?

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:43.910
The modifications
are too extensive.

00:19:44.016 --> 00:19:47.076
Their neuronal pathways
have been fundamentally altered.

00:19:47.152 --> 00:19:48.346
You hold the key.

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:50.115
Why?

00:19:50.189 --> 00:19:51.747
You were there with us.

00:19:51.823 --> 00:19:54.223
Planet 1865 Alpha.

00:19:54.293 --> 00:19:55.590
You must remember.

00:19:57.763 --> 00:20:00.789
Eight years ago,
our vessel crashed.

00:20:00.866 --> 00:20:03.130
The four of us were
the only survivors.

00:20:03.202 --> 00:20:04.794
When we were reassimilated...

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:07.338
We found we'd been linked
together somehow.

00:20:07.406 --> 00:20:09.636
We were a subset
within the collective.

00:20:09.708 --> 00:20:12.438
It's like having three voices
whispering in one ear...

00:20:12.511 --> 00:20:14.570
And a crowd screaming
in the other.

00:20:14.646 --> 00:20:17.410
We had to break free,
so we worked together,

00:20:17.482 --> 00:20:18.915
and we finally escaped.

00:20:18.984 --> 00:20:21.475
We had our implants removed
on Inavar Prime...

00:20:21.553 --> 00:20:23.384
But they couldn't break
the neural link.

00:20:23.455 --> 00:20:24.945
We need to find out

00:20:25.023 --> 00:20:26.752
what happened eight years ago

00:20:26.825 --> 00:20:28.156
after the crash...

00:20:28.227 --> 00:20:31.788
The night we were reassimilated
into the collective.

00:20:31.863 --> 00:20:34.957
We need to know how
the link was created.

00:20:35.067 --> 00:20:36.967
But our memories are...

00:20:37.035 --> 00:20:39.629
Fragmented, disorganized.

00:20:39.705 --> 00:20:42.902
We hoped that you would know.

00:20:42.975 --> 00:20:45.136
I don't.

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:49.579
However, I am willing to attempt
to retrieve the data.

00:20:51.483 --> 00:20:54.077
Come with me.

00:21:01.526 --> 00:21:02.686
Are you ready?

00:21:04.596 --> 00:21:05.563
Yes.

00:21:08.267 --> 00:21:10.531
Data search complete.

00:21:10.602 --> 00:21:12.797
Do you remember
anything further?

00:21:13.872 --> 00:21:15.100
No.

00:21:17.276 --> 00:21:18.470
My last memory is of us...

00:21:18.543 --> 00:21:19.874
Is of us standing around...

00:21:19.945 --> 00:21:20.877
Around a campfire.

00:21:20.946 --> 00:21:22.072
And yet the data files

00:21:22.147 --> 00:21:25.173
in your cortical processor
appear to be intact.

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:26.774
I see no evidence
that would explain

00:21:26.852 --> 00:21:28.342
your lapse in memory.

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:29.614
What about you?

00:21:29.688 --> 00:21:32.418
Why don't you remember
what happened?

00:21:32.491 --> 00:21:33.423
I don't know.

00:21:33.492 --> 00:21:34.959
I've found no evidence

00:21:35.093 --> 00:21:37.618
of damage
to my memory files either.

00:21:37.696 --> 00:21:39.288
I remember the campfire

00:21:39.364 --> 00:21:41.958
and then waking up
in the collective.

00:21:42.034 --> 00:21:43.899
There is an obvious gap...

00:21:43.969 --> 00:21:45.732
but no indication of why.

00:21:45.804 --> 00:21:48.204
Why do they still
call you Seven?

00:21:48.273 --> 00:21:50.104
You should have a name.

00:21:50.175 --> 00:21:51.107
It is my name.

00:21:51.176 --> 00:21:52.108
No.

00:21:52.177 --> 00:21:55.169
It's a designation.

00:21:55.247 --> 00:21:57.112
You're an individual now.

00:21:58.350 --> 00:22:02.514
I decided that my former name
was no longer appropriate.

00:22:02.587 --> 00:22:05.920
Prepare to reinitialize
the memory cascade.

00:22:06.058 --> 00:22:08.458
I can't wait to use
my real name again.

00:22:08.527 --> 00:22:11.553
There is nothing
preventing you from doing so.

00:22:11.630 --> 00:22:13.530
Except that, most of the time,

00:22:13.598 --> 00:22:18.194
I don't know whether my name
is Marika, P'Chan or Lansor.

00:22:18.270 --> 00:22:19.601
The names, the memories...

00:22:19.671 --> 00:22:22.834
The memories, even the thoughts
flow from one to the other.

00:22:22.908 --> 00:22:24.535
I can't love or hate or laugh...

00:22:24.609 --> 00:22:26.338
- Or cry without...
- or cry without...

00:22:26.411 --> 00:22:28.538
- sharing it with them.
- Sharing it with them.

00:22:28.613 --> 00:22:31.673
How can any of us take
a name for ourselves...

00:22:31.750 --> 00:22:32.944
For ourselves?

00:22:33.018 --> 00:22:34.849
We're not individuals.

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:36.217
We're not Borg.

00:22:36.288 --> 00:22:37.915
We're nothing.

00:22:40.292 --> 00:22:42.692
Begin the memory cascade.

00:22:54.840 --> 00:22:56.432
"A friendly game"?

00:22:56.508 --> 00:22:58.635
Well... that's how it started.

00:22:58.710 --> 00:23:01.702
I see. And perhaps you
could explain to me

00:23:01.780 --> 00:23:04.840
how this friendly game
turned into a street brawl?

00:23:04.916 --> 00:23:08.113
Well, Harry and I
wanted to explore the station.

00:23:08.186 --> 00:23:09.676
Um... we wanted to broaden

00:23:09.755 --> 00:23:12.519
our understanding
of alien cultures and, uh...

00:23:12.591 --> 00:23:14.115
Skip the recruiting speech.

00:23:14.192 --> 00:23:15.591
You were looking for a bar.

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:16.786
Then what?

00:23:16.862 --> 00:23:17.920
Well, we found one

00:23:18.029 --> 00:23:20.497
and we met a pair
of Kinbori who told us

00:23:20.565 --> 00:23:22.089
about this game they play

00:23:22.167 --> 00:23:24.533
with these big,
odd-looking rackets...

00:23:24.603 --> 00:23:26.434
You mean one of those?

00:23:27.606 --> 00:23:28.868
Yeah!

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:30.066
Yeah.

00:23:30.142 --> 00:23:32.110
L-in any case,
they challenged us

00:23:32.177 --> 00:23:33.769
to a game and we accepted,

00:23:33.845 --> 00:23:37.144
but I guess we weren't quite
aware of all the rules.

00:23:37.215 --> 00:23:38.773
Because you'd been drinking.

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:40.841
Yes, ma'am.

00:23:40.919 --> 00:23:43.513
Y-You see, we thought
it was a version of tennis,

00:23:43.588 --> 00:23:45.681
but as soon as we
hit the first volley,

00:23:45.757 --> 00:23:47.657
this Kinbori jumps over the net

00:23:47.726 --> 00:23:49.785
and starts attacking
us with his racket.

00:23:49.861 --> 00:23:52.091
So we figured we were
supposed to fight back...

00:23:52.164 --> 00:23:53.131
Yeah.

00:23:53.198 --> 00:23:54.688
And then, uh...

00:23:54.766 --> 00:23:57.132
well, things got
a little out of hand.

00:23:57.202 --> 00:23:59.466
"A little out of hand."

00:23:59.538 --> 00:24:04.134
Seven Voyager crewmen,
including two Bridge officers

00:24:04.209 --> 00:24:09.374
along with 13 Kinbori
and one Morphinian cafe owner...

00:24:09.448 --> 00:24:10.847
all arrested.

00:24:10.916 --> 00:24:12.907
The charges range
from disorderly conduct

00:24:12.984 --> 00:24:15.077
to assault
on a security officer.

00:24:15.153 --> 00:24:17.246
Th-That one's not true.

00:24:17.322 --> 00:24:18.516
Oh, thank you, Mr. Kim.

00:24:18.590 --> 00:24:20.421
I'll note that exception
in my log.

00:24:20.492 --> 00:24:23.052
You're both confined to quarters
until further notice...

00:24:23.128 --> 00:24:25.062
after you report to Sick Bay.

00:24:25.130 --> 00:24:26.358
That's all.

00:24:29.100 --> 00:24:30.965
Well, did you win?

00:24:32.404 --> 00:24:33.928
Oh, yes, ma'am.

00:24:34.005 --> 00:24:36.872
We kicked their... rackets.

00:24:36.942 --> 00:24:38.204
Good.

00:24:38.276 --> 00:24:39.334
Dismissed.

00:24:43.148 --> 00:24:44.240
Any progress?

00:24:44.316 --> 00:24:46.147
I've determined that we all have

00:24:46.218 --> 00:24:48.379
exactly the same gap
in our memories.

00:24:48.453 --> 00:24:51.320
It seems unlikely
that it would be a coincidence.

00:24:51.389 --> 00:24:53.050
So you believe the collective

00:24:53.124 --> 00:24:55.285
deliberately wiped
your recollections

00:24:55.360 --> 00:24:57.157
of the reassimilation process?

00:24:57.229 --> 00:24:58.958
It is the most
likely explanation.

00:24:59.097 --> 00:25:00.155
But?

00:25:00.232 --> 00:25:01.790
The collective would not care

00:25:01.867 --> 00:25:04.495
that four drones remembered
being reassimilated.

00:25:04.569 --> 00:25:07.037
Something must have happened
during the process.

00:25:07.105 --> 00:25:09.073
Something they wanted
to hide from you.

00:25:09.140 --> 00:25:12.200
Let's look at this from
a different perspective.

00:25:12.277 --> 00:25:13.835
Why would the collective

00:25:13.912 --> 00:25:16.813
lock them into a neural triad
in the first place?

00:25:16.882 --> 00:25:17.814
I don't know.

00:25:17.883 --> 00:25:19.510
There is no advantage
to having three drones

00:25:19.584 --> 00:25:20.710
linked together in this manner.

00:25:20.785 --> 00:25:23.219
Well, they obviously did
it for some reason...

00:25:23.288 --> 00:25:25.256
and I get the feeling
that if we can answer

00:25:25.323 --> 00:25:27.917
that question, the rest
should fall into place.

00:25:28.026 --> 00:25:29.789
But I wish we could find a way

00:25:29.861 --> 00:25:32.056
to close the gaps
in your memories.

00:25:34.599 --> 00:25:36.066
There is a way.

00:25:36.134 --> 00:25:40.093
I assume there's a reason you
didn't mention it before now.

00:25:40.171 --> 00:25:43.038
It would involve linking
my neural interface to theirs.

00:25:43.108 --> 00:25:45.838
Together, we may be able
to restore the missing data.

00:25:45.911 --> 00:25:48.379
However, I would again
be part of a group mind.

00:25:48.446 --> 00:25:52.712
You're not eager to revisit
that experience, hmm?

00:25:52.784 --> 00:25:54.581
There's also the possibility

00:25:54.653 --> 00:25:57.679
that I could become trapped
in the neural link.

00:25:57.756 --> 00:25:59.781
Turning the triad
into a quartet.

00:25:59.858 --> 00:26:02.520
I won't ask you to take
that kind of risk.

00:26:04.229 --> 00:26:06.720
I do feel compelled
to help them,

00:26:06.798 --> 00:26:11.201
but I am uncertain as to
the correct course of action.

00:26:13.772 --> 00:26:16.434
Let me ask you something.

00:26:16.508 --> 00:26:21.002
Do you think of these people...
as family?

00:26:23.248 --> 00:26:25.239
Is it relevant?

00:26:25.317 --> 00:26:26.614
There's an old saying:

00:26:26.685 --> 00:26:28.482
"Blood is thicker than water."

00:26:28.553 --> 00:26:30.384
It means that the ties of family

00:26:30.455 --> 00:26:33.253
run deeper than any other
kind of relationship.

00:26:33.325 --> 00:26:36.055
We'll often do things
for members of our family

00:26:36.127 --> 00:26:40.223
we'd never dream of doing
for anyone else.

00:26:45.937 --> 00:26:48.531
Seven! Seven!

00:26:48.607 --> 00:26:49.733
Naomi Wildman.

00:26:49.808 --> 00:26:51.503
I heard about the drones.

00:26:51.576 --> 00:26:52.804
Did they hurt you?

00:26:52.877 --> 00:26:55.141
I am not damaged.

00:26:55.213 --> 00:26:57.147
What do they want?

00:26:57.215 --> 00:27:00.207
They are seeking
information from me,

00:27:00.285 --> 00:27:03.812
but I am uncertain
whether I can help them.

00:27:03.888 --> 00:27:05.253
Oh. Be careful.

00:27:06.891 --> 00:27:11.487
Naomi Wildman,
do you consider me to be family?

00:27:13.231 --> 00:27:16.826
I... I don't, I mean...

00:27:16.901 --> 00:27:18.835
well...

00:27:18.903 --> 00:27:20.495
yes.

00:27:20.572 --> 00:27:23.040
Is... that okay?

00:27:23.108 --> 00:27:25.838
I have no objection.

00:27:25.910 --> 00:27:29.471
Do you... think of me as family?

00:27:31.249 --> 00:27:32.682
Yes.

00:27:37.288 --> 00:27:39.381
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:27:39.457 --> 00:27:42.290
Seven of Nine has decided
to undergo the procedure

00:27:42.360 --> 00:27:44.658
that will link her mind
with the other drones.

00:27:44.729 --> 00:27:46.162
Despite the risk involved,

00:27:46.231 --> 00:27:49.894
she feels an obligation to help
these "distant cousins."

00:27:49.968 --> 00:27:52.163
I'll be monitoring
your neural readings

00:27:52.237 --> 00:27:53.636
while you're in the link.

00:27:53.705 --> 00:27:55.502
But I'm not certain I'll be able

00:27:55.573 --> 00:27:58.133
to counter the effects
if... you become trapped.

00:27:58.209 --> 00:27:59.767
I know you'll do your best.

00:27:59.844 --> 00:28:01.141
It's never a good sign

00:28:01.212 --> 00:28:04.477
when the patient feels the need
to comfort the Doctor.

00:28:04.549 --> 00:28:06.517
Good luck.

00:28:13.925 --> 00:28:16.223
- Ready.
- Ready.

00:28:16.294 --> 00:28:17.921
- Ready.
- Ready.

00:29:15.120 --> 00:29:16.712
You are damaged.

00:29:16.788 --> 00:29:18.380
I will assist you.

00:29:21.626 --> 00:29:24.060
Don't worry.

00:29:24.129 --> 00:29:26.154
Everything will be all right.

00:29:49.921 --> 00:29:52.116
The collective has located us.

00:29:52.190 --> 00:29:54.215
A Borg vessel is on its way.

00:29:54.292 --> 00:29:56.226
We will be one
with the Borg again.

00:29:56.294 --> 00:29:59.058
No! I do not want
to rejoin the collective.

00:29:59.130 --> 00:30:00.324
Agreed.

00:30:00.398 --> 00:30:02.923
That is in violation of
all established protocols.

00:30:03.034 --> 00:30:04.126
Forget the protocols.

00:30:04.202 --> 00:30:05.169
You're not a drone.

00:30:05.236 --> 00:30:06.498
You're a person, like us.

00:30:06.571 --> 00:30:07.538
You have a name...

00:30:07.605 --> 00:30:09.197
a life!

00:30:09.274 --> 00:30:11.834
All you have to do is embrace
who you really are.

00:30:11.910 --> 00:30:13.400
No. I do not exist.

00:30:13.478 --> 00:30:16.345
I am only part
of the greater whole.

00:30:16.414 --> 00:30:17.711
That's what they
want you to believe.

00:30:17.782 --> 00:30:19.215
That's what they want
us all to believe.

00:30:19.284 --> 00:30:20.512
We are Borg.

00:30:20.585 --> 00:30:23.349
Our primary function
is to serve the collective.

00:30:23.421 --> 00:30:25.719
Not anymore.

00:30:29.661 --> 00:30:32.186
Error! Input failure!

00:30:32.263 --> 00:30:34.254
They may know what planet we're
on, but without the beacon,

00:30:34.332 --> 00:30:35.697
it'll be far more difficult
to locate us.

00:30:35.767 --> 00:30:37.792
If we can remodulate
our cortical implants,

00:30:37.869 --> 00:30:39.803
we might be able
to elude their sensors.

00:30:39.871 --> 00:30:41.600
We must leave this place.

00:30:41.673 --> 00:30:44.608
This discussion is in violation
of all established protocols.

00:30:51.382 --> 00:30:53.111
You stay here

00:30:53.184 --> 00:30:55.516
and be reassimilated
if you want to.

00:30:55.587 --> 00:30:56.952
I won't!

00:32:02.487 --> 00:32:04.751
What are you... doing?

00:32:04.822 --> 00:32:08.019
The nanoprobes
will create new interlink nodes

00:32:08.092 --> 00:32:09.582
in your left hemisphere.

00:32:09.661 --> 00:32:12.129
Resistance is futile.

00:32:58.376 --> 00:32:59.434
I will not comply!

00:33:01.713 --> 00:33:03.681
I will not comply!

00:33:14.459 --> 00:33:16.393
State your designations.

00:33:16.461 --> 00:33:20.625
Two of Nine,
Primary Adjunct of Unimatrix 01.

00:33:20.698 --> 00:33:21.687
Three of Nine,

00:33:21.766 --> 00:33:24.929
Auxiliary Processor
of Unimatrix 01.

00:33:25.003 --> 00:33:26.061
Four of Nine,

00:33:26.137 --> 00:33:28.901
Secondary Adjunct
of Unimatrix 01.

00:33:28.973 --> 00:33:30.770
What is your primary function?

00:33:30.842 --> 00:33:32.400
To serve the collective.

00:33:32.477 --> 00:33:35.105
You will repair
the communications beacon.

00:33:40.284 --> 00:33:41.376
It was you!

00:33:41.452 --> 00:33:42.476
You were responsible.

00:33:42.553 --> 00:33:43.815
What have you done to us?

00:33:43.888 --> 00:33:44.820
You linked us together.

00:33:44.889 --> 00:33:46.413
You're responsible
for our suffering.

00:33:46.491 --> 00:33:47.549
How could you do it?

00:33:47.625 --> 00:33:49.252
If you didn't want to return...

00:33:49.327 --> 00:33:51.090
- To the collective...
- You didn't have to.

00:33:51.162 --> 00:33:52.686
You don't understand
what happened.

00:33:55.767 --> 00:33:57.200
Somebody help me!

00:33:58.803 --> 00:33:59.735
What's happening?

00:33:59.804 --> 00:34:01.465
Somehow, they broke
their link with Seven.

00:34:01.539 --> 00:34:02.471
They're malfunctioning.

00:34:02.540 --> 00:34:03.700
Help me get them to Sick Bay.

00:34:07.979 --> 00:34:09.446
When they broke
the connection with you,

00:34:09.514 --> 00:34:12.347
it must have overloaded
their cortical implants.

00:34:12.417 --> 00:34:14.817
They went into neural shock.

00:34:14.886 --> 00:34:17.252
And yet I was undamaged.

00:34:17.321 --> 00:34:20.381
I think I know why.

00:34:20.458 --> 00:34:22.323
You said you remembered
injecting them

00:34:22.393 --> 00:34:24.088
with nanoprobes
eight years ago...

00:34:24.162 --> 00:34:26.153
Yes.

00:34:26.230 --> 00:34:28.630
It created an interlink
between them.

00:34:28.699 --> 00:34:30.394
It was the only way
to prevent them

00:34:30.468 --> 00:34:31.867
from escaping the collective.

00:34:31.936 --> 00:34:34.905
Well, it seems to have had
an unfortunate side effect.

00:34:34.972 --> 00:34:36.496
Their higher brain functions

00:34:36.574 --> 00:34:38.565
were somehow tied
into the interlink.

00:34:38.643 --> 00:34:41.840
When they broke their connection
with you in the Cargo Bay,

00:34:41.913 --> 00:34:44.711
the shock to their cognitive
systems was too great.

00:34:44.782 --> 00:34:46.079
Can you revive them?

00:34:46.150 --> 00:34:48.948
I could remove
the microcortical implants.

00:34:49.020 --> 00:34:51.511
That would break the link
binding them together,

00:34:51.589 --> 00:34:53.113
but it would also kill them.

00:34:53.191 --> 00:34:55.056
They'd only live
a matter of weeks.

00:34:55.126 --> 00:34:56.718
A month at the most.

00:34:56.794 --> 00:34:58.955
What are the other options?

00:35:00.865 --> 00:35:02.992
They could be returned
to the Borg.

00:35:03.067 --> 00:35:05.365
If they were reassimilated
into the collective,

00:35:05.436 --> 00:35:06.994
they would regain consciousness

00:35:07.071 --> 00:35:08.902
and then live out
a normal life span.

00:35:09.006 --> 00:35:10.268
As drones.

00:35:10.341 --> 00:35:13.640
As drones,
but they'd be alive, Seven.

00:35:22.920 --> 00:35:24.478
They have no hope of surviving

00:35:24.555 --> 00:35:26.455
unless they return
to the collective.

00:35:26.524 --> 00:35:29.357
Not exactly a happy ending,
is it?

00:35:29.427 --> 00:35:30.416
No.

00:35:32.263 --> 00:35:34.288
Back on that planet...

00:35:34.365 --> 00:35:36.390
why do you think
you reacted so differently

00:35:36.467 --> 00:35:37.525
from the rest of them?

00:35:37.602 --> 00:35:39.797
Why were you so afraid
of becoming an individual?

00:35:41.806 --> 00:35:44.366
When I was first assimilated
into the collective,

00:35:44.442 --> 00:35:47.809
I was a child.

00:35:47.879 --> 00:35:49.938
They were assimilated
as adults.

00:35:50.081 --> 00:35:53.744
When our individual memories
began to resurface...

00:35:53.818 --> 00:35:55.809
Yours were of being
a little girl...

00:35:55.887 --> 00:35:58.014
a scared little girl.

00:35:59.891 --> 00:36:02.382
I let that fear control me.

00:36:03.628 --> 00:36:05.755
After I saw the drone
die in the swamp,

00:36:05.830 --> 00:36:08.663
I... panicked.

00:36:08.733 --> 00:36:11.600
I began to envision
my own death...

00:36:11.669 --> 00:36:13.466
alone...

00:36:13.538 --> 00:36:17.269
without even the sound of
another drone to comfort me.

00:36:17.341 --> 00:36:20.902
So I forced them to return.

00:36:21.012 --> 00:36:24.243
I infiltrated their left
cerebral hemispheres

00:36:24.315 --> 00:36:27.307
with nanoprobes and created
a new interlink network...

00:36:27.385 --> 00:36:29.444
one that they couldn't resist.

00:36:29.520 --> 00:36:32.819
And then I eliminated
the evidence of what I'd done.

00:36:32.890 --> 00:36:34.255
You were overwhelmed by feelings

00:36:34.325 --> 00:36:35.792
you couldn't begin
to understand.

00:36:35.860 --> 00:36:37.589
You're not responsible for that.

00:36:37.662 --> 00:36:39.721
Because of what I did,
they'll be forced to live

00:36:39.797 --> 00:36:41.924
the rest of their lives
in the collective.

00:36:42.033 --> 00:36:43.432
For that, I am responsible.

00:36:48.906 --> 00:36:51.204
There's a difference
between surviving and living.

00:36:51.275 --> 00:36:53.800
They'll survive
in the collective,

00:36:53.878 --> 00:36:56.073
but they won't really be alive.

00:36:56.147 --> 00:36:58.012
You know that better
than any of us.

00:36:59.083 --> 00:37:01.517
There is no alternative.

00:37:01.586 --> 00:37:03.577
How long would they survive

00:37:03.654 --> 00:37:06.088
if the Doctor deactivated
this...

00:37:06.157 --> 00:37:08.091
interlink network you created?

00:37:08.159 --> 00:37:09.683
A month at most.

00:37:11.429 --> 00:37:14.364
A month as an individual
or a lifetime as a drone.

00:37:16.133 --> 00:37:19.591
Which option would you choose?

00:37:30.081 --> 00:37:33.448
Survival is insufficient.

00:37:33.517 --> 00:37:35.314
I beg your pardon?

00:37:35.386 --> 00:37:37.684
Eight years ago, I forced them
to return to the collective.

00:37:37.755 --> 00:37:40.121
I won't make
the same mistake again.

00:37:40.191 --> 00:37:44.150
They deserve to exist
as individuals.

00:37:44.228 --> 00:37:46.594
We must terminate the link
between them.

00:37:48.966 --> 00:37:50.831
I understand that you feel
a certain responsibility

00:37:50.901 --> 00:37:52.266
for these patients.

00:37:52.336 --> 00:37:55.533
But as their physician, so do I.

00:37:55.606 --> 00:37:57.073
It's my duty
to preserve their lives

00:37:57.141 --> 00:37:59.439
for as long as possible,
even if that means...

00:37:59.510 --> 00:38:01.603
I will not return them
to the Borg.

00:38:01.679 --> 00:38:05.342
Are you thinking of what's best
for them... or for you?

00:38:05.416 --> 00:38:07.577
Clarify.

00:38:07.652 --> 00:38:08.880
You've said it yourself.

00:38:08.953 --> 00:38:10.045
You made a mistake.

00:38:10.121 --> 00:38:12.988
And Seven of Nine doesn't like
to make mistakes.

00:38:13.057 --> 00:38:15.184
She strives for perfection.

00:38:15.259 --> 00:38:19.195
I want you to think about the
motivation behind your decision.

00:38:19.263 --> 00:38:22.596
Are you doing what's right
for those three people...

00:38:22.667 --> 00:38:25.261
or are you trying to alleviate
the guilt you feel

00:38:25.336 --> 00:38:27.167
over what happened
eight years ago?

00:38:28.739 --> 00:38:32.539
The damage I did
can never be repaired,

00:38:32.610 --> 00:38:35.306
and my guilt is irrelevant.

00:38:35.379 --> 00:38:42.114
I simply want them to experience
individuality... as I have.

00:38:42.186 --> 00:38:43.813
As you have.

00:38:43.888 --> 00:38:47.016
At one time, you were
confined to this Sick Bay.

00:38:47.091 --> 00:38:51.494
Your program was limited to
emergency medical protocols.

00:38:51.562 --> 00:38:54.861
In some ways, you were not
unlike a drone.

00:38:54.932 --> 00:38:57.298
But you were granted
the opportunity

00:38:57.368 --> 00:38:58.665
to explore your individuality.

00:38:58.736 --> 00:39:00.567
You were allowed
to expand your program.

00:39:00.638 --> 00:39:04.768
Your mobile emitter gives
you freedom of movement.

00:39:04.842 --> 00:39:07.106
Your thoughts are your own.

00:39:07.178 --> 00:39:08.509
If you were told

00:39:08.579 --> 00:39:12.538
you had to become a drone again,
I believe you would resist.

00:39:13.818 --> 00:39:17.185
Yes, I suppose I would.

00:39:17.254 --> 00:39:19.688
They would resist as well.

00:39:19.757 --> 00:39:24.456
They would choose freedom,
no matter how fleeting.

00:39:26.764 --> 00:39:30.666
Only you and I can truly
understand that.

00:39:30.735 --> 00:39:34.603
Survival is insufficient.

00:39:45.683 --> 00:39:48.675
It's so... quiet.

00:39:51.856 --> 00:39:54.825
I had no idea
you were going to say that.

00:39:57.728 --> 00:40:00.322
I don't know what either of you
is thinking.

00:40:02.666 --> 00:40:04.634
I'd forgotten what it was like

00:40:04.702 --> 00:40:06.932
to be alone
with my own thoughts.

00:40:10.941 --> 00:40:12.272
I'm leaving.

00:40:12.343 --> 00:40:14.436
Where will you go?

00:40:14.512 --> 00:40:17.709
I want to see the space station.

00:40:17.782 --> 00:40:20.945
To meet new people.

00:40:21.085 --> 00:40:23.280
To fill my life...

00:40:23.354 --> 00:40:25.618
with life again...

00:40:28.025 --> 00:40:29.993
in the time I have left.

00:40:55.653 --> 00:40:58.349
I'm leaving as well.

00:40:58.422 --> 00:41:01.391
There's an uninhabited planet

00:41:01.459 --> 00:41:04.792
only a few light-years
from here.

00:41:04.862 --> 00:41:10.664
I'd like to spend my final days
in the open air.

00:41:26.150 --> 00:41:31.349
My people don't believe
in holding grudges.

00:41:31.422 --> 00:41:35.290
I wish you well, Seven of Nine.

00:41:35.359 --> 00:41:37.827
Thank you.

00:41:48.372 --> 00:41:53.901
It's nice to be on a
Federation starship again.

00:41:53.978 --> 00:41:56.845
I'd like to stay
aboard Voyager.

00:41:56.914 --> 00:42:00.406
The Captain said you may
stay as long as you wish.

00:42:00.484 --> 00:42:02.918
You mean as long as I have.

00:42:05.289 --> 00:42:09.020
I can't forgive you
for what you did to us.

00:42:11.061 --> 00:42:13.791
But I do understand
why you did it.

00:42:30.180 --> 00:42:31.738
Naomi Wildman.

00:42:31.815 --> 00:42:35.216
I thought you might
like some company.

00:42:35.286 --> 00:42:36.878
Why?

00:42:36.954 --> 00:42:39.218
Because of... what
happened with the drones.

00:42:39.290 --> 00:42:43.226
I see that word travels quickly.

00:42:43.294 --> 00:42:45.762
It's a small ship.

00:42:45.829 --> 00:42:49.697
I thought maybe you might want
to spend some time with...

00:42:49.767 --> 00:42:51.758
family.
